    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d268">

                <pb facs="0374" n="208" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg208"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.811/239</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Reinsch to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-01-11T18:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1917, 6 p.m</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In spite of the views of the Department indicated in your telegram January 8, 5
                    p.m., Corporation has instructed its representatives here to secure as soon as
                    possible Chinese approval of Japanese participation in canal projects.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
